menuconfig DRIVERS_SECURE_ELEMENT_SE050
	bool "se050 (NXP EdgeLock)"
	default n
	---help---
		NXP SE050 secure element over I2C.

		Provides a PX4 module 'se050' with 'start|stop|status'
		subcommands. 'se050 start' registers the NuttX /dev/se05x
		character device on the configured I2C bus.

		Must be started AFTER any slow (100 kHz-only) devices on the
		same bus have finished their one-shot init, because SE050 uses
		a per-transfer 400 kHz clock override.

		Requires NuttX defconfig options (not auto-selectable from the
		PX4 Kconfig tree):
		    CONFIG_CRYPTO=y
		    CONFIG_DEV_SE05X=y
		    CONFIG_DEV_SE05X_PLAIN=y  (or CONFIG_DEV_SE05X_SCP03=y)

		When disabled the module is not built and callers must fall
		back to a traditional software-based flow.
